REMARK   1   O   egfr-siteA-id73           80 aa  de novo design
REMARK   1
REMARK   1 HOW THE CHAINS WERE BROUGHT INTO ONE FRAME
REMARK   1   Each binder was predicted in its own complex with its own
REMARK   1   copy of the receptor. Chain R is the receptor copy from the
REMARK   1   egfr-siteA-id2015 complex, so THAT binder sits against chain R
REMARK   1   EXACTLY as predicted. Every other binder was brought in by
REMARK   1   superposing its own receptor copy onto chain R, which was then
REMARK   1   discarded; its contacts with chain R therefore carry that fit's
REMARK   1   error. The exact predicted geometry for a binder is in its own
REMARK   1   per-design complex, where one is deposited; otherwise it is in
REMARK   1   the raw predictions, which are too large to distribute.
REMARK   1
REMARK   1 SITE A (chain R, WT numbering):
REMARK   1   380 382 384 408 409 410 411 412 417 438 465
REMARK   1 SITE B (chain R, WT numbering): 19 20 21 25 28 29 50
REMARK   1
